(a) Prior to placing or using dumpsters or commercial trash receptacles within the corporate city limits of the City of Ringgold by any person or business, any person or business desiring to place and/or use such dumpsters or commercial trash receptacles shall make application for, and obtain from the city, a permit authorizing such placement and/or use.
(b) Application for permit shall be made to the city manager, or his designee, on forms approved by the city.
(c) Upon application, the city manager, or his designee, shall issue a permit as set forth herein upon a showing by the applicant that the following standards will be satisfied:
(1) The dumpster or commercial trash receptacle will not be situated on any curb or roadway or otherwise block any portion of a motorway or pose a hazard to or otherwise interfere with traffic;
(2) The dumpster or commercial trash receptacle will not be situated at or so near to an intersection as to create an actual or potential safety hazard; under no circumstance shall a dumpster be within 25 feet of an intersection;
(3) The dumpster or commercial trash receptacle will not encroach upon the curb or any other paved portion of any right-of-way of the City of Ringgold unless the applicant makes a showing of hardship, based on the special conditions of the property in question or for reasons of health and safety, that it cannot so comply as determined by the mayor and council;
(4) The dumpster or commercial trash receptacle will be maintained in accordance with the rules and regulations of the Catoosa County Health Department;
(5) Foul odors emanating more than 50 feet from the dumpster or commercial trash receptacle will be quelled within a reasonable time of the person's or business' notice thereof;
(6) Leakage, trash, and litter arising from the dumpster or commercial trash receptacle will be cleaned up within a reasonable time of occurrence;
(7) Only materials allowed by state law will be placed in the dumpster or commercial trash receptacle;
(8) No residential or commercial garbage from outside the city limits will be deposited anywhere within the city limits, including dumpsters and commercial trash receptacles; and
(9) All dumpsters or commercial trash receptacles shall be enclosed with solid fencing, walls, and/or other barriers such that visibility of and emission of odors from each dumpster or commercial trash receptacle is minimized. Nothing in this subsection is intended or shall be constructed to interfere with the placement or removal of trash from any dumpster or commercial trash receptacle.
(d) The applicant must further submit to the city manager, or his designee, a site plan indicating the proposed location of the dumpster or commercial trash receptacle, which shall include the name, address and telephone number(s) of the dumpster or commercial trash receptacle owner, the leasing party, and the servicing company.
(e) Exception to the requirements herein may be made only in cases of hardship and shall be determined by the mayor and council.
(f) Existing dumpster or commercial trash receptacles must make an application and comply within thirty (30) days of receiving notification of this section except as otherwise provided in subsection (e).
(g) Any property damage incurred by the city as the result of the use of any dumpster or commercial trash receptacle, including, but not limited to damage to the pavement, sidewalks, curbs, utilities, shall be the responsibility of and shall be repaired or otherwise remedied to the satisfaction of the city by the owner of the dumpster or commercial trash receptacle.
(h) Violations of this section shall be punishable as set forth in section 1-11 herein and/or the city may seek an injunction or pursue whatever legal remedies it deems necessary to enforce the provisions of this Code section.
(Ord. No. 06-0327-01, § 1, 3-27-06)

